 "notes": "Stretch 2: p.120 all rows (Ch. II rows 1-6, rule, Ch. IX rows 7-9) and p.121 rows 1-6 to 'maāχeru' above the long rule. Line numerals: Ch. II - '1.' before Re (p120 r1); '2.' before the second 'à' (p120 r2); '3.' printed inside àreruti after D4:D21 (p120 r4, word kept in line 2); '4.' before the second Àusàr (p120 r5). Ch. IX - '1.' before Re (p120 r7); '2.' before māk-à (p120 r8); '3.' before àtef-f (p120 r9); p121: '4.' before àtef...-à (r2), '5.' before un-nà (r3), '6.' before sāḥ-kuà (r4). Overlines: the thick rule over each chapter title is ruled directly over the title groups: Ch. II from Re to àn (it stops before Àusàr, which is not rubric); Ch. IX from Re to àn. No other overlines in the stretch. The thin rule under the running head is not an overline. Budge's '(sic)' stands after the second Àusàr (D4 Q1 A40) on p120 row 5 (line 4). Square brackets in the sign line: p120 r2 around Ani's determinative A1; p121 r2 around the second seated figure of àtef...-à; p121 r5 around G43 Z1 of āper-kuà. Dots: p121 r2 transliteration 'àtef . . . - à' (recorded as printed). Brackets only in English: '[and]' (ānχ), '[Osiris]' (after t'eṭ àn, no sign), '[my] father'. p120 r6: a small broken mark precedes 'ta' in the transliteration. The flat sign with slanted left end open at right is coded Aa15 throughout (em, mit, àmmehet); the closed form in maāχeru Aa11. Ani's determinative in this type is a kneeling man with a raised forearm (no flail visible): coded A1. The tall upright with small tie marks on its left (in āba, sāḥ, χu) coded Y1a."
